20% of 100 is 20. So, the new box has 100 + 20 = 120 pods. The cost per pod for the regular box is $12/100 = $0.12. The cost per pod for the new box is $12/120 = $0.10. With the $12 regular box, you can run 100 cycles (100 pods / 1 pod per cycle). With the $12 new box, you can run 120 cycles (120 pods / 1 pod per cycle).

Therefore, you can run 120 cycles.

\boxed{120}

First, we need to determine how many face masks Johnny bought. The problem states that Johnny bought 2 more than thrice as many as Mike. "Thrice as many as Mike" means 3 times the number of masks Mike bought. Mike bought 5 face masks, so 3 times that number is 3 * 5 = 15.  Then, Johnny bought 2 more than this, so we add 2 to 15. 15 + 2 = 17. 

Therefore, Johnny bought 17 face masks.

\boxed{17}
